From 1e1df03d6304e1dca61e5a7625e8caee46eebc3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:51:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a ledger write that records a real approval is
 recognized, and its card says what it is

Smart approval held a ledger close whose note said "Jacob: yes to ..." as if the user never approved, and the card named neither the entry nor where the claimed approval came from.

Cause: a compaction handoff row was read as a User line. The summary body (written by a model) was shown as the user's words and cut at 4,000 characters, before the decision ledger that the handoff carries at its end, so the user's yes that a compaction had folded away was never shown. Now the summary body is never a user line. The review lists what Hermes itself kept of the user: the ledger's USER, PAGE, STEER and CLARIFY entries with the question each answered, and the verbatim quotes section of the handoff (a ledger block counts only while compression.decision_ledger_chars is above 0), plus the user's own text merged into a handoff row. Agent notes, dispatches, open questions, a subagent's handoff and a handoff-looking tool or system row are never listed. Chat grants no longer read a summary's body as a user message either.

A ledger write that only records state (list, search, a question, dispatched work, a release, a plain note or close) is no longer reviewed. One that records a decision or claims what the user approved is reviewed, skips the cheap stage 1 (Sonnet's stage 1 let a note through when the chat held nothing the user said), and carries a harness note saying such a record needs the user's own words for that same thing. Its card now names the entry (id, kind, status, text, the question it answers), the note it records, and the user's closest statement with its source (message, answer to a question card, or words kept through a compaction) and time, or says that nothing matches.
